      friendship: 0
  - title: What would you do?
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - A man from the tower came to the door this morning. In a suit, on Walt's porch!
    - He wants to buy my recipe and sell my bread at the counter. My name on the bag. More money than I've ever seen.
    - Or... Ada says we should do what they used to do in the city. A Saturday market in the plaza. Everyone bringing what they make.
    - You're a sensible one. What would you do?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Start a Saturday market
      replyA:
      - A market! Yes. Ada with her flowers, Soo-ah with her seeds, Mi-sook with her kimchi. And you, dear, with everything you grow.
      - I'll tell Walt to build the stalls. He'll grumble for a week and then make them perfect.
      flagsA:
      - suburb_market_planned
      optionB: Sell the recipe to the tower
      replyB:
      - You're right. I'm old, and it's a great deal of money, and Walt's knee isn't getting better.
      - My name on a bag. Fancy that. I'll ring the man in the morning.
      flagsB:
      - rosa_sold_recipe
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Market day
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Did you see it? Did you SEE it? Six stalls! Walt built every one of them and complained the whole time.
    - Ada sold out of tulips by ten. Mi-sook gave away more kimchi than she sold. And my bread was gone before the pigeons were awake.
    - Bring your best crops next Saturday. I've saved you the stall by the fountain.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: My name on a bag
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 2
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I saw my bread at the tower yesterday. In plastic. With my name on it, spelled wrong.
    - It doesn't taste like mine. They changed the flour to make it cheaper. I asked and they said it's 'the same recipe, optimised'.
    - I've stopped baking at home. There doesn't seem much point now, does there?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Tomas comes home
    number: 10
    heartsNeeded: 10
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - You'll never guess who walked through the market on Saturday. In a suit, looking for the bakery counter.
    - Tomas. He'd heard about the market at the tower and came to see what was stealing their customers.
    - He ate a whole loaf standing at my stall. And then he complained about my soup. Oh, it was wonderful.
    - He's coming for Sunday dinner. And Sam is coming too. I asked them myself. Thank you, dear. For all of it.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags:
    - suburb_market_open
    reward:
      gold: 500
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The oven's warm again
    number: 10
    heartsNeeded: 10
    path: 2
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I tore up the contract. Walt says I'll be sued. I said let them sue an old woman with a rolling pin.
    - 'And look who came round when he heard: Tomas. He said the tower bread tastes like the bag it comes in.'
    - So I'm baking again, dear. One loaf for every house, the old way. And one for Sam, with soup, every Sunday, on the step.
    - Some things you shouldn't sell. I'm only sorry it took me so long to remember.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
